## File changes not showing live

- [x] 12. Explorer tree and open editor tabs miss file changes (agent edits, terminal, e.g. `python -m venv .venv`) — intermittent, desktop AND server
  - FIXED: creating/removing .venv/build/etc. itself is reported; watcher errors/overflow emit `rescan: true` (tree re-reads cached dirs, open tabs re-check); case-insensitive path matching on Windows; server sends a rescan to a lagged WebSocket client; symbol-index updates now run in the flush thread instead of the notify callback (Cause C); a watcher that fails to start keeps a placeholder entry and retries in the background every 10s for ~5 min, stopping when the project is closed (Cause D).
  - Both platforms share one watcher: crates/rustic-app/src/watcher.rs (whole project, batched `rustic:fs-change` every ~300 ms). Agent writes emit no event of their own — everything depends on this watcher.
  - Cause A (certain for .venv): WATCHER_SKIP_DIRS (watcher.rs:13-31) includes .venv, venv, build, dist, out, tmp, target, node_modules, and the filter drops the folder ITSELF, not just its contents (watcher.rs:252). So creating .venv/build/dist never refreshes the parent -> folder never appears; open files inside them never reload.
  - Cause B (likely the "sometimes"): watcher errors and rescan signals are ignored (`if let Ok(event) = res`, watcher.rs:203). Big bursts (venv, pip/npm install, git checkout) overflow the Windows event buffer -> whole batch lost silently, including unrelated agent edits, no rescan. The other watcher (crates/rustic-agent/src/file_history/watcher.rs) already handles overflow/rescan.
  - Cause C: symbol-index work runs inside the notify callback while holding the lock (watcher.rs:268-276), slowing event draining and making overflow more likely.
  - Cause D: a watcher that fails to start (watcher.rs:280-299) is never retried (e.g. after cloud-sync re-watch).
  - Cause E (editor tabs): fsChangeTouchesPath (src/lib/use-file-change.js:18-33) compares paths exactly — drive-letter/case differences on Windows miss the reload. Tabs with unsaved edits intentionally don't reload (monaco-editor.jsx:453).
  - Cause F (server only): hub broadcast channel of 1024 (rustic-server/src/lib.rs:180) shared with agent streaming; a lagging client skips ahead (ws.rs:39-40) and loses fs-change events, with no resync on skip/reconnect.
  - Fix plan: report create/remove of skipped folders themselves (filter only paths inside them); on Err/rescan log it and emit a "rescan all" fs-change that refreshes cached tree dirs + open tabs; move index work out of the callback; retry failed watchers and surface errors; case-insensitive path compare on Windows; server rescan on lag/reconnect; optionally have agent file tools emit fs-change for the paths they write.

## Git / GitHub

- [x] 13. GitHub username not shown on some computers, although sync/pull/push work
  - FIXED: github_get_user falls back to `gh auth token` then non-interactive `git credential fill` (crates/rustic-git/src/identity.rs, desktop + server); frontend always tries and retries on window focus.
  - Cause: the name comes only from GitHub /user using Rustic's OWN stored token (src/state/github.js:39-46 -> github_get_user, src-tauri/src/commands/git.rs:939-962, rustic-server/src/commands/git.rs:912-938). Push/pull without that token fall back to the system git credential helper (crates/rustic-git/src/remote.rs:37-59), e.g. Git Credential Manager / SSH / gh — so git works but no username.
  - Also: keychain load failure is ignored (src-tauri/src/lib.rs:202-204); /user errors are swallowed (github.js:45) and shown as a bare "GitHub"; init() runs once with no retry (github.js:36-37), so an offline start leaves it empty all session; web server stores the token per server data dir.
  - Fix plan: backend `github_identity` fallback chain — Rustic token -> `gh auth token` -> non-interactive `git credential fill` (GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0, GCM_INTERACTIVE=never) -> /user; last resort remote-URL user / `git config user.name` (name only). Log keychain failures, show an error state instead of "GitHub", retry on focus/online.

## Terminal

- [x] 14. Side-panel terminal text vanishes with Antigravity / Claude Code / Codex (comes back on scroll)
  - FIXED: terminal repaints (clear glyph atlas + refresh) when it becomes visible again (IntersectionObserver), after real resizes, on window focus / tab visibility / DPR change, and after WebGL context loss (terminal-instance.js). Needs confirmation on an affected machine.
  - Screenshot: .rustic/uploaded/pasted-image-2.png — text replaced by blank/solid blocks.
  - Cause: xterm WebGL renderer (@xterm/addon-webgl, src/components/terminal/terminal-instance.js:169-175, 366-398) draws from a stale glyph atlas after the panel is hidden/resized/GPU cache drop. The repaint() helper (clear atlas + full refresh, terminal-instance.js:529-533) only runs when a pane's `active` flips (terminal-pane.jsx:204-220) or when scrolling into history (terminal-instance.js:480-495). The side panel mounts the pane with `active` hard-coded true (src/components/agent/cli-chat-view.jsx:131), so it never repaints after being hidden/shown. Resize (refit) never repaints; no visibilitychange/focus/DPR handling; onContextLoss disposes WebGL without refreshing (terminal-instance.js:370-377).
  - Why scroll fixes it: scrolling triggers the atlas clear/refresh, or (alternate screen) makes the TUI redraw everything.
  - Fix plan: pass a real visibility signal (or IntersectionObserver) to TerminalPane in cli-chat-view; repaint after real size changes (debounced); repaint on visibilitychange / window focus / DPR change; on context loss refresh + refit (optionally re-create WebGL).
  - Quick confirm on an affected machine: localStorage['rustic.terminal.renderer']='dom' — if text stops vanishing, it's the WebGL atlas.

